      "message": "I definitely agree with that goal and approach [of explicitly copying the struct when required], and that is what I had in mind when writing this CL.\n\nMy only reservation about doing it using an aligned struct is that I was not confident that we could say for certain exactly what the compiled code would end up looking like, and that we could never have a regression through some change in toolchain, hence opting for this somewhat clumsy but explicit approach.\n\nThat said, I agree that if we can achieve the same level of certainty in C (John suggested compiler intrinsics, though we didn\u0027t find a suitable one yet) that would be nicer, I\u0027m just not sure how to do that :)",
